met:
With the winds and the waves and the flowers at play;
And she met with a youth of gentle air,
With the light of the sunshine on his hair.

metallic:
My heath lay farther off, where lizards lived
In strange metallic mail, just spied and gone;
Like darted lightnings here and there perceived

methought:
Descended the celestial nine;
O'er me methought they deign'd to shine,
And deign'd to string my lyre.
